Yves,

After looking more closely at the accompanying R syntax for Savalei & Yuan (2009) <http://www2.psych.ubc.ca/~vsavalei/>, it seems like it may be easy to adapt it into a function for semTools.  I'm working on this simulation presently, so I'm going to write a function that accepts raw data and model-implied moments (potentially fit outside of R), does one of the 3 transformations (a user-specified argument), and returns bootstrapped samples, optionally with an option to export data to file(s) for analysis in another package.  Then I'll write a wrapper which allows the user simply to fit the target model to the data, and then pass the fitted lavaan object to the wrapped function (or OpenMx object).  Since their new method is not widely available (still only in EQS?), it would be a flexible tool for applied researchers using any software, including lavaan.  And that might save you some time for other developments :-)  Of course, if you still want to include this functionality in lavaan, I wouldn't complain, but I could also make a wrapper for the wrapper, which accepts model syntax and data, along with other lavaan arguments (similar to the runMI functions), and has extra arguments for which transformation, max iterations, etc.

If I don't run into any trouble, I should make a push to github within the next week.  Thanks for all your work!

Terry

