Mark--
     You are correct.  If a variable is dependent, then that specification fixes the residual variance, not the total variance.  The total variance of a dependent variable is not a model parameter, but you can standardize all factors with the std.lv <http://std.lv> option on the command (cfa, sem, lavaan) that you use to estimate the model.
--Ed Rigdon

